This scenario is quite exceptional, I think it could be useful for the user to handle this. If they trigger this, it is because they are doing something uncommon. If we just return false, it could be quite hard to diagnose.

I'm not entirely sure about the conventions here regarding exceptions in `TryFormat` methods. However, `decimal.TryParse` can throw a `System.FormatException` for example:
```C#
Span<char> aSpan = stackalloc char[50];
decimal aDecimal = 1;
string anInvalidFormat = "a";
aDecimal.TryFormat(aSpan, out int b, anInvalidFormat);
```

